    <section class="secao">
      <h2>DATA QUALITY</h2>
      <ul>
        <li class="linha"><strong>EMPTY STATE</strong><p>The state column is empty in 100% of rows. The state was derived from the first two digits of the IBGE code of the hospital's municipality.</p></li>
        <li class="linha"><strong>SPLIT ICD</strong><p>The main diagnosis comes in two columns, depending on the code length. Using only one, 90% of admissions would have no diagnosis, so both were combined.</p></li>
        <li class="linha"><strong>2024 AND 2025</strong><p>2024 has duplicated months and 2025 has missing months, so the analysis covers 2015–2023.</p></li>
        <li class="linha"><strong>VALIDATION</strong><p>Totals by state and by year match (107,368,293 admissions in both), as do the yearly sums of each diagnosis and the overall ranking.</p></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

